Q6. What are wrapper classes in Java?
Convert primitive data types to objects (Integer, Double, Boolean, etc.)

Q7. Explain Autoboxing and Unboxing?
Autoboxing: primitive → Wrapper Object automatically.
           eg- int num = 10;          // primitive
               Integer obj = num;     // autoboxing happens automatically
            Note:- You didn’t call new Integer(num), but Java did it behind the scenes.
Unboxing: Wrapper Object → primitive automatically.
           eg- Integer obj = 20;      // wrapper object
               int num = obj;         // unboxing happens automatically
           Note:- You didn’t call obj.intValue(), but Java did it internally.

