Q19. WHY JAVA IS NOT 100% OBJECT – ORIENTED ?
Java is called object-oriented, but not 100% OOP because it has some features that are not objects.
- Primitive Data Types : Java has 8 primitive types (int, float, double, char, boolean, byte, short, long).In a pure OOP language, everything should be an object.
- Static Methods and Variables : Static members belong to the class, not to an object. however everything should be tied to an object.
- Main Method : The main() method is static, It runs without creating an object of the class, which violates pure OOP principles.

Q20. Why is the main() method static in Java?
By declaring main method as static to allow JVM to call main method directly without creating instance of the class.

