Q1. What is Garbage Collector in Java?
In java , garbage collector is a component of JVM which automatically keeps on removing 
objects from heap memory on regular bases which are not in use which helps to avoid overflow 
of memory and memory management becomes efficient. 

Q2. Which JVM is most commonly used in Java applications?
“HOTSPOT” is the most commonly used JVM by oracle, All hotspot’s GC implements generational GC strategy

Q3. What are different Garbage Collectors in HotSpot JVM?
- Serial GC → Single-threaded, for small apps.
- Parallel GC → Multi-threaded, high throughput.
- CMS (Concurrent Mark-Sweep) → Low pause collector (deprecated after Java 9).
- G1 GC (Garbage First) → Default since Java 9, balances pause + throughput.
- ZGC / Shenandoah → Ultra-low pause collectors (Java 11+).

Q4. Which Garbage Collector is default in Java 8 vs Java 11 vs Java 17?
- Java 8 → Parallel GC (default).
- Java 9+ → G1 GC (default).
- Java 11+ → G1 GC (default, but ZGC available).
- Java 17 → G1 GC default, ZGC highly used in modern apps.

Q5. How does Garbage Collection work internally?
👉 Two steps: Marking (identify unreferenced objects) + Deletion (remove them).

Q6. What is Generational Garbage Collection?
👉 GC divides heap into Young Generation, Old Generation, and PermGen/Metaspace.
- Young → short-lived objects
- Old → long-lived objects
- PermGen/Metaspace → class metadata

Q7. Why generational strategy?
👉 Because most objects are short-lived (e.g., method-local variables).

Q8. Can you force Garbage Collection in Java?
the developer cannot force it, only request it (System.gc() or Runtime.getRuntime().gc()).

Q9. What is difference between finalize() method and Garbage Collector?
👉 finalize() is called before GC deletes an object (but not guaranteed). It’s deprecated in Java 9+.

Q10. What is memory leak in Java if GC is automatic?
👉 Memory leak still happens if objects are referenced but never used, so GC cannot collect them. Example: storing objects in a static list but never removing them.

Q11. Does Garbage Collector collect objects from stack?
👉 No. GC only works on heap memory, not stack.









